# DTF tier manifest: debian-rpm-maintenance
# Profile-set: filesystem / single.
#
# THE BUGS (all main-only: the Debian backfill (#4905) and the precomputed
# RPM repodata builder (#5067) are not on the 1.11 line)
#   #5082 POST /api/v1/admin/repositories/{key}/backfill-debian with
#         dry_run: true did not check where a misfiled package would move.
#         A package whose pool/main/ destination held a different package, a
#         trashed row, or the move of another misfiled copy was counted in
#         packages_registered/packages_relocated by the dry run, while the
#         real run refused it (artifacts_failed). Fixed by #5083.
#   #5088 the same endpoint: a misfiled copy merged into a same-bytes
#         destination row that is itself a candidate. The dry run counted the
#         package again when the destination came up on a later candidate
#         page (500 rows by id), so it reported more packages_registered than
#         the real run; on the same page both modes counted it twice. Fixed by
#         #5212.
#   #5072 hosted RPM precomputed repodata: after a repository's storage_path
#         changed, the builder deleted superseded revisions only through the
#         new location, so revisions written to the previous location stayed
#         there for ever. Fixed by #5210.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   Backfill candidates (.deb rows with no Debian control document, the
#   pre-#4657 migrated shape) are generic uploads of real .debs built by
#   fixtures/build_deb.py, with any `debian` artifact_metadata row of those
#   uploads deleted (psql). Taken destinations are native Debian uploads, one
#   moved to the trash. #5088 adds 1000 filler candidates and adds pairs until
#   the random id order holds a pair split across candidate pages and a pair
#   on one page. #5072 moves the repository the way an operator does (copy
#   the objects, repoint storage_path with psql: no API changes a location)
#   and forces two builds through the rebuild endpoint.
#
# RED/GREEN
#   red:   ak-backend:sha-c7a9ada (main 2026-10-29, before #5083/#5212/#5210:
#          every FIX case fails), ak-backend:sha-12808b8 (main 2026-11-02, has
#          #5083: red for #5088 and #5072 only)
#   green: ak-backend:sha-9d3aa45 (main, has #5083, #5212 and #5210)
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~1100 uploads and the admin calls through one user.
COVERS="5082 5088 5072"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
